@startuml
title Dynamics, Cockpit Control and Telemetry

skinparam shadowing false

actor Operator
participant "Cockpit QML" as Cockpit
participant "CockpitControlService" as Controls
participant "MovementIntent" as Intent
participant "FlightDynamicsEngine" as FDE
participant "Dynamics backend" as Backend
participant "Entity" as Entity
participant "Telemetry builders" as Telemetry
participant "Cesium / PFD / ECAM" as Views

Operator -> Cockpit: change heading / altitude / speed
Cockpit -> Controls: neutral setpoint command
Controls -> Intent: update desired values

loop simulation tick owned by runtime
  FDE -> Intent: resolve active task, plan or cockpit intent
  Intent --> FDE: desired heading / altitude / speed

  alt JSBSim configured and healthy
    FDE -> Backend: step(simulationTime, deltaTime, setpoints)
    Backend --> FDE: position / attitude / speed / systems
  else kinematic backend or fallback
    FDE -> Backend: integrate bounded kinematics
    Backend --> FDE: position / attitude / speed
  end

  FDE -> Entity: commit canonical state
  Entity -> Telemetry: build immutable snapshots
  Telemetry -> Views: kinematics and systems telemetry
end

note over Cockpit,Controls
The UI emits commands.
It never owns the physics state.
end note

note over Backend,Entity
Fuel exhaustion and backend failure
are explicit runtime states/events.
end note

@enduml
